WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Model Y's sales leadership in South Korea and Taiwan shows Tesla holding ground in key Asian markets, even as rivals push new models. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 593. In Taiwan, the Model 3 recorded 949 deliveries during August, while the Model Y added 788 registrations. The two models together reached 1,737 units for the month. Year to date, the pair has surpassed

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:53.440
12,550 deliveries, and remains well ahead of the nearest competitor. The Model Y alone has accumulated 9,315 registrations in Taiwan this year, compared with 2,511 for Toyota's BZ4X. The Model 3 added 3,243 registrations to hold second place in overall annual volume.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:01:12.580
In South Korea, the same crossover finished first among all passenger cars sold last month. It held the top imported car ranking for the seventh straight month amid continued preference from local buyers through repeat purchases. That performance came even as other brands increased their China-made offerings in the market.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:21.100
While sales momentum builds in Asia, Tesla is also pushing regulatory progress on autonomy through a different kind of transparency.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:36.880
Tesla shared detailed safety data to support its push for European FSD approval. The company published crash statistics and opened its dashboard for external review. This approach differs from competitors that have released less granular information.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:48.820
Regulators received concrete data sets rather than summary claims alone. The level of disclosure aims to provide evidence of incremental improvement across software versions and hardware updates.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:02:01.380
That same focus on real world performance shows up in independent safety testing closer to home. The Model Y received the Insurance Institute for Highway Safety's highest safety rating for the current model year.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:13.980
The award covers tested configurations and reflects strong results in crashworthiness and crash avoidance evaluations. This recognition adds to the vehicle's established safety profile in independent testing.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:20.080
Even as the crossover collects safety honors, a manufacturing issue prompted a targeted recall.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:32.400
Tesla issued a recall for specific Model Y units already in customer hands due to a suspension fastener issue. The action requires service visits to correct the installation of the fastener.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:41.980
The recall addresses a potential manufacturing variance in placement. This step comes as the company prepares for higher production volumes of the refreshed model.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:53.660
On the autonomy side, real world incidents are raising fresh questions about responsibility. An influencer forwarded a speeding citation directly to Tesla after an FSD incident.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:03:04.300
The citation followed a traffic violation that occurred while the supervised system was active. The move highlights ongoing questions about liability assignment during system operation.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:16.580
Not every comparison favors Tesla right now. Uber and Waymo already operate driverless services in select cities, while Tesla's unsupervised timeline remains the most uncertain of the group.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:22.580
Sightings of driverless cybercabs in Austin prompted residents to track the vehicles across the city.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:29.640
Night testing at Giga, Texas included low light runs focused on sensor performance without traditional steering controls.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:42.920
The session's demonstrated preparation for varied lighting scenarios ahead of wider deployment. Korean customers continue to show strong loyalty through repeat purchases and positive sentiment toward the brand and service network.

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:53.140
A passenger sat in a gold-colored cyber cab without realizing the manufacturer, illustrating how quickly the new design blends into city streets during expanded testing.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:04:06.460
Stepping back from the data, one segment looks at how these technical choices affect the bigger picture. Hyundai's battery retained over 93% health after 93,000 miles in the largest study of its kind.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:18.320
The analysis of 500,000 tests placed Tesla behind in the long-term degradation ranking. The result highlights measurable differences in battery longevity performance across manufacturers.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:24.940
The study provides one of the most extensive data sets available on real-world electric vehicle battery health.

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:30.540
Safety data disclosure is becoming a quiet differentiator in autonomous driving approvals.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:39.660
Tesla's decision to publish detailed crash statistics and allow external review gives regulators a concrete data set rather than summary claims.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:46.340
That transparency can shorten approval cycles when agencies need evidence of incremental improvement over time.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:52.480
The choice also creates a public record that can be tracked across software versions and hardware updates.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:59.620
Competitors often release only high-level safety reports or rely on internal audits that stay behind closed doors.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:05.880
Tesla's approach trades some short-term public relations risk for faster regulatory feedback loops.

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:13.360
The trade-off appears in markets where agencies have already signaled they want raw numbers before granting unsupervised operation.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:20.400
In Europe, this strategy is being tested directly as the company seeks FSD clearance with the shared information.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:30.960
Over the longer term, this choice affects how quickly Tesla can scale Robotaxi services versus rivals that treat safety documentation as a defensive exercise.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:39.840
If the data continues to show measurable gains, the same openness that invites scrutiny today could become the baseline requirement for everyone else.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:46.280
The outcome will influence not only Tesla's timeline, but the standards applied to the entire driverless sector.

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:54.520
Before we go, watch for further updates on how the European safety data sharing affects the next steps in FSD regulatory review.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.400
That covers it for today's Tesla developments.

